1
00:00:01,330 --> 00:00:03,750
Go for it! Kitasumi for the win!

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:05,750
We need to shore up our 
defense in the middle!

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,710
Taro, don't do anything stupid this time!

4
00:00:10,110 --> 00:00:11,580
I won't let him past me this time.

5
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,880
I didn't do all that defensive 
practice for nothing!

6
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:16,080
It doesn't matter how 
much height he has on me!

7
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:21,700
You dumbass! She told us
to expect shots from long range!

8
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:23,660
Momoharu, get the rebound!

9
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:25,500
Shit, you guys are running me ragged!

10
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:29,750
Loose ball!

11
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,710
What the hell?!

12
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:32,340
You had one job, Momoharu!

13
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,760
Not happening!

14
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:38,760
Crap... he waited to shoot...!

15
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:48,060
That little snot... he took his sweet time
to get the foul call!

16
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:49,890
Defensive foul on #7!

17
00:00:49,890 --> 00:00:52,030
The basket counts! One free-throw!

18
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,200
He made a complete fool 
out of me in front of Nao.

19
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,170
Damn him and his silky seaweed hair!

20
00:01:01,170 --> 00:01:03,160
I'm gonna totally murder him!

21
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:05,130
One free-throw!

22
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,040
Dear God,

23
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:12,460
I love Nao with all my heart.

24
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:15,720
So if the power of love truly does exist...

25
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:20,580
...then please help me tap into it now!

26
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:53,170
Ahiru no Sora

27
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:03,920
The Best Start and the Worst Start

28
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:07,080
Shit! I swear I must be losing my damn mind!

29
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:09,880
I'm seriously starting to 
think that dude is cool!

30
00:03:11,370 --> 00:03:14,380
Taro! Why the hell are you 
praying before a free-throw?!

31
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:17,090
5 more seconds and it 
would have been a penalty!

32
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:19,330
Listen up, boys!

33
00:03:19,330 --> 00:03:22,830
We'll never live it down if we lose
to a hair oil addict like that chump!

34
00:03:22,830 --> 00:03:24,050
We know.

35
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:27,560
Don't let them catch up. 
Let's lay on the pressure.

36
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:28,270
Right!

37
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:31,540
Defense! Defense! Defense!

38
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:34,080
Defense! Defen- huh?

39
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:39,210
Defense! Defense! Defense!

40
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:36,250
Wait, aren't we on offense right now?

41
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:39,210
If you don't know what you're 
doing, then stop doing it!

42
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:41,500
Here they come!

43
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,500
Konishi! Watch out for #4!

44
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,290
On him!

45
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:51,080
You've got the ball, but what 
can you even do from here?

46
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:53,670
I'm not just going to leave 
you open for an easy shot!

47
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:02,710
How the hell does he turn on a dime
while running so fast?!

48
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,040
He blocked the shot!

49
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,140
Nice, Taro!

50
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:15,880
Tell me, is there a reason
you aren't trying to score any baskets?

51
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:16,610
Huh?

52
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:19,240
First you screwed up that 
jump ball and now this.

53
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:21,070
Have you forgotten how to play the game?

54
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:23,250
Konishi, you damn punk.

55
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:26,130
Are you just here to start 
shit with me or what?

56
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:27,210
I'm disappointed.

57
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:31,750
Because I had been really looking forward
to playing against you, Senpai.

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,870
Even back then, you were...!

59
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:41,510
Shit, was he always this good?!

60
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:46,420
I'm gonna shut you down hard!

61
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,210
Nice pass, Koney!

62
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:59,210
Awesome play, Taro! Konishi!

63
00:04:56,920 --> 00:05:00,630
Kitasumi

64
00:04:56,920 --> 00:05:00,630
Kuzuryu

65
00:04:59,210 --> 00:05:00,630
That evens up the score!

66
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:04,920
Damn.

67
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:16,920
Defense! Defense! Defense!

68
00:05:06,210 --> 00:05:08,630
Come on, freshmen!
I know you can cheer louder than that!

69
00:05:09,330 --> 00:05:11,540
They're starting to build 
up some serious momentum.

70
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:13,330
We need to score a basket soon.

71
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:16,920
They haven't gotten to the point
of totally dominating the game.

72
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:19,210
But letting them take the lead 
here would be really bad!

73
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:25,300
We've gotta push through 
and sink a shot right now!

74
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:31,540
Gah! I can't believe I let him get me
with that lame-ass fake!

75
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:33,750
Koney! Help me out!

76
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:39,290
Oh crap!

77
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,460
You left me wide open.

78
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:45,780
Damn! I've got to stop him, 
even if it means a foul!

79
00:05:46,130 --> 00:05:48,330
I'm gonna pay you back 
for that fake you pulled.

80
00:05:48,330 --> 00:05:49,630
And with interest!

81
00:05:53,290 --> 00:05:54,750
A dunk?!

82
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,840
A-are you all right?

83
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:06,210
SHIT! I WAS SO CLOSE!

84
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:08,550
Just a little more and I 
would have touched the rim!

85
00:06:08,550 --> 00:06:11,210
You mean he didn't touch the rim just now?

86
00:06:11,210 --> 00:06:13,380
So then, that was just his 
attempt to fake a dunk?

87
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,850
But wow, he got some 
serious air on that jump.

88
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:18,590
Anybody who plays basketball has to satisfy

89
00:06:18,590 --> 00:06:21,820
the urge of pulling off a dunk 
during a game, at least once!

90
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:24,820
Dude, you can't even pull it off to begin with.
The rim's too high.

91
00:06:25,580 --> 00:06:27,880
If I was just 5 centimeters taller...

92
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:32,000
I told you. The only winner here is me.

93
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:35,120
I'll admit that your three-pointers 
are pretty impressive,

94
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,700
but they're not enough to win.

95
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:40,530
Just so you know, it's not 
our height that separates us.

96
00:06:40,530 --> 00:06:42,670
The crucial difference 
between you and me is...

97
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:47,080
...the fact that I have wings, and you don't.

98
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,590
Bye-bye, baby.

99
00:06:50,590 --> 00:06:53,050
Defense! Defense! Defense!

100
00:06:53,050 --> 00:07:00,630
Defense! Defense! Defense!

101
00:06:53,250 --> 00:06:56,390
What now? The other team
is starting to really get riled up.

102
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:58,850
Let's go defense! Get it done!

103
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,000
Out of bounds! Kitasumi ball!

104
00:07:07,210 --> 00:07:09,460
Timeout by Kuzuryu High!

105
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:14,170
Kitasumi
Kuzuryu

106
00:07:09,790 --> 00:07:12,580
I didn't realize Kitasumi 
was so tough to beat.

107
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:15,380
I don't think we can win, not at this rate.

108
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:20,210
It's a little early, but we're going
to change up our defense.

109
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:23,580
The players that we need 
to shut down are #7...

110
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:27,800
...and #14 when he goes to post up.

111
00:07:29,710 --> 00:07:31,790
Although he hasn't made any shots yet,

112
00:07:31,790 --> 00:07:34,010
we also need to look out for 
dribble penetration from #5.

113
00:07:35,750 --> 00:07:38,670
That all being said, we're actually
in a pretty good position.

114
00:07:38,670 --> 00:07:41,550
Going up against this team is 
the perfect opportunity to put

115
00:07:41,550 --> 00:07:43,230
the defense we practiced into use.

116
00:07:43,790 --> 00:07:45,170
Do you understand?

117
00:07:45,170 --> 00:07:48,420
This is going to be where the 
real trial for our team starts.

118
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,430
It's going to be hard for you out there,

119
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:54,160
but you're the cornerstone 
of our defense, Kurumatani.

120
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:58,580
A'ight! Let's knock their socks off.

121
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:02,040
And show them what our 
defense is really made of!

122
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:08,710
Kurumatani will need to return back
to doing footwork practice by himself tomorrow.

123
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:14,460
What will decide the outcome of this match
is whether you can stop him or not.

124
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:19,630
I'll stop him, no matter what!

125
00:08:23,250 --> 00:08:25,690
What's this? Their defense changed.

126
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:26,750
Huh?

127
00:08:28,830 --> 00:08:31,480
That little guy rushed out all on his own!

128
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,150
Full court man-to-man?!

129
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,240
Have you gone off the deep end?!

130
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,830
But the four in the back are doing zone?

131
00:08:39,830 --> 00:08:43,660
That's Box and 1, no... it's 
actually Diamond and 1!

132
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:46,740
Hmm. So, they let the short one run loose

133
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:49,420
and kept their tallest player 
at the top of the zone.

134
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:52,630
It's a solid formation that 
fully accounts for our offense.

135
00:08:52,630 --> 00:08:55,960
However... it's much easier said than done.

136
00:08:57,250 --> 00:08:59,330
I wonder just how long they'll last?

137
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,300
This is the same defense
the girls' team used against us, isn't it?

138
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,670
That's right.

139
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:07,290
The formation is a little different, 
but the idea is the same.

140
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:11,040
Tinytown is going to get wiped out
doing full court, ain't he?

141
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:14,960
I mean, the offense doesn't really
make any moves until they reach the front court.

142
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,750
And that's exactly why it's necessary.

143
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:19,380
Before they even reach front court,
our goal is to make them think

144
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:25,170
"#7 can't do anything", or even just,
"getting a pass to him would be difficult."

145
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:30,330
Like you said, this is really going
to push the limits of Kurumatani's stamina.

146
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:34,330
But our opponent will be expending
just as much effort by trying to shake him.

147
00:09:35,290 --> 00:09:38,290
We'll throw their scorer off-kilter
with pressure and fatigue.

148
00:09:38,290 --> 00:09:40,210
That will be Kurumatani's job.

149
00:09:41,170 --> 00:09:44,130
Of course, it won't be easy for 
the rest of the team, either.

150
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:47,790
Since they'll be playing zone D
with only 4 players instead of the typical 5.

151
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:51,750
Okay, but like, are you really sure
that our defense is so important?

152
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:56,500
I feel like we could easily win this thing
if Kite and Sora just focused on scoring.

153
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:58,820
Yeah, I was thinking about that, too.

154
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:02,520
It's true that the effectiveness 
of defense is ambiguous,

155
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:05,540
we can't just tally it 
like points or rebounds.

156
00:10:06,210 --> 00:10:10,500
That also makes it difficult to understand
how much of an impact it has on the end result.

157
00:10:11,130 --> 00:10:13,630
However, I think that only applies
if you ignore one important thing.

158
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:16,880
The reality of winning or losing.

159
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:21,290
The majority of players on losing teams
share the same feelings after a game,

160
00:10:21,290 --> 00:10:23,670
about how essential defense 
is to winning the game.

161
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:27,330
That was close, I gotta focus.

162
00:10:27,330 --> 00:10:30,850
There's no point to using this defense
if I let Kabachi get free.

163
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:34,380
I've gotta be quick to fill any space
where a pass might come through.

164
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:39,290
But the problem is, this guy is really good
at subtle fakes and other simple moves.

165
00:10:40,210 --> 00:10:42,080
He's also a lot quicker 
on his feet than I am.

166
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:43,330
But even so...

167
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:44,790
Too slow!

168
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:48,380
Why do you keep using defensive slides against me
when I'm doing a full-on drive?

169
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:50,000
Didn't you consider just 
dashing alongside me?

170
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:53,340
No, because then it'll 
delay my reaction time.

171
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:56,240
You dummy. Your ability to 
react in time only matters

172
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:58,800
if you can actually keep up with your mark.

173
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:01,880
Your priority is to match 
the speed of your opponent,

174
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:05,250
or move slightly faster than them
if they have possession of the ball.

175
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,880
If you can't do that,
then we'll never be able to use Nanao's defense.

176
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:11,670
All right, let's go again.

177
00:11:14,630 --> 00:11:16,860
Dealing with an opponent 
who is unbelievably fast...

178
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:19,580
...that's something I'm totally 
used to at this point!

179
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:22,070
And compared to how 
ridiculously fast Kite is...

180
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:24,210
...this guy seems way 
more grounded in reality!

181
00:11:25,830 --> 00:11:27,490
He's gotten pretty damn good.

182
00:11:27,490 --> 00:11:29,960
Dammit! It's like he's stuck right to me!

183
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:34,590
I hate sticky shit like natto 
and gum with a passion!

184
00:11:34,590 --> 00:11:37,300
I can do this! I can shut him down!

185
00:11:37,710 --> 00:11:38,540
Screen!

186
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,130
Kato! Pass it to m-

187
00:11:49,170 --> 00:11:50,080
Behind you, Nabe!

188
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,040
Huh?

189
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:54,530
Nice shot!

190
00:11:54,530 --> 00:11:59,170
Kitasumi

191
00:11:54,690 --> 00:11:57,710
Kitasumi! Kitasumi!

192
00:11:57,710 --> 00:12:01,080
Katori! Nice assist!

193
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:05,620
That's the way. Create some open space
and then attack their weak side.

194
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:07,770
Don't sweat it, Nabe!

195
00:12:07,770 --> 00:12:09,950
Just shake it off and switch to offense!

196
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:12,170
You okay after that run in?

197
00:12:12,830 --> 00:12:13,920
Your head hit my elbow pretty hard.

198
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:15,880
I'm fine!

199
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:25,500
Defense! Defense! Defense!

200
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,590
Only 3 minutes left in the first quarter.

201
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:22,430
That settles it! For the 
rest of this quarter...

202
00:12:22,430 --> 00:12:24,800
I won't let Kabachi score a single point!

203
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:26,880
Rebound!

204
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:31,080
Kitasumi!

205
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,380
Let's score!

206
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:33,920
There's an opening near #8, hurry!

207
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:37,040
Hey, am I crazy or is Momoharu 
a little off his game?

208
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:39,750
You think? There's not much
he could've done differently just now.

209
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,210
Him again?!

210
00:12:45,210 --> 00:12:46,710
Dammit, what a pest!

211
00:12:47,210 --> 00:12:51,170
I don't want to boost their morale
by letting them shut Taro out here.

212
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:54,790
So we'll catch them off guard by getting Taro
to score with brute force.

213
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:57,960
Shit!

214
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:01,050
I don't get it. How is he so relaxed
while putting up such a fierce defense?

215
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:03,580
Having a solid poker face is 
essential to a good defense!

216
00:13:04,170 --> 00:13:06,260
I can't afford to show him even
the slightest sign of fatigue!

217
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:10,220
Rather than staying up close, I'm better off
leaving a tiny bit of space between us.

218
00:13:10,670 --> 00:13:12,430
No matter what crazy moves 
he pulls to get rid of me,

219
00:13:12,430 --> 00:13:13,930
I can't let my eyes of the ball.

220
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:16,270
I've got to keep track of the 
point guard's movement, too.

221
00:13:16,270 --> 00:13:20,630
Kuzuryu
Kitasumi

222
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:20,630
Actually, wait... I don't have the time
to be thinking about all that right now!

223
00:13:21,130 --> 00:13:24,710
I just need to sprint, dash... 
and run all over the place!

224
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:34,630
You might think you've got me 1-on-1,
but from my eyes it's 5-on-1!

225
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:43,200
This is the same situation as before!

226
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,040
Kato!

227
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:47,430
I've got this!

228
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:50,600
What the?!

229
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,500
That damn shrimp!

230
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,360
Out of bounds! Kitsumi ball!

231
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,790
Aw, man! I was so close!

232
00:14:02,790 --> 00:14:05,300
I knew having a shorty would be useless.

233
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:07,130
What a waste of space.

234
00:14:07,130 --> 00:14:09,040
Let's swap him out for Yashuhara.

235
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:10,870
No way, I won't stand for it!

236
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:13,000
That was almost a clean steal.

237
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:16,080
Yeah, it would have been
a huge advantage if he'd gotten it.

238
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,420
There's nothing to be disappointed about.

239
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:20,670
Throw-in!

240
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:24,210
He's providing us with the very best defense!

241
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:34,330
Sweet! That's the third one in a row!

242
00:14:34,330 --> 00:14:35,710
Nice moves, Kite!

243
00:14:40,250 --> 00:14:43,290
I can't believe they're sticking to Taro
for the entire quarter.

244
00:14:43,290 --> 00:14:44,980
There's hardly any time left!

245
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:47,750
Go Kitasumi! Sink it before the buzzer!

246
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:51,120
Don't make it sound so easy!

247
00:14:55,790 --> 00:14:58,330
That's the end of the first quarter!

248
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:00,500
2-minute interval!

249
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,920
Hey Sora, great job out there!

250
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:06,630
Thanks!

251
00:15:06,630 --> 00:15:10,090
Kuzuryu
Kitasumi

252
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:08,710
They haven't left us in the dust.

253
00:15:08,710 --> 00:15:10,090
We're keeping right up with them!

254
00:15:10,710 --> 00:15:13,430
And most importantly, Kabachi hasn't 
scored a single basket since

255
00:15:13,430 --> 00:15:15,310
I started my full court defense!

256
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,000
I did it!

257
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,770
I shut him down!

258
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:21,480
We can do this! We can win!

259
00:15:24,790 --> 00:15:29,150
He's drenched in sweat,
and they're not even at halftime yet.

260
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:32,210
You know, I'm starting think 
we're pretty damn good!

261
00:15:32,210 --> 00:15:36,240
The score might be tied, but I think
we've showed them who has the most skills!

262
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,920
Kite's actually scored more 
than I thought he would!

263
00:15:39,790 --> 00:15:42,710
Well, it looks like you guys
aren't going to need me to save you.

264
00:15:43,330 --> 00:15:46,500
We've barely made it 1/4th 
of the way through the match.

265
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:49,920
Things are only going to get harder for us
from here on out.

266
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:54,130
I have here a copy of their team's
official records from last year.

267
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:58,600
National High School Basketball Tournament 
Kanagawa Preliminaries  - Kitasumi

268
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:58,600
Kitasumi is what is known 
as a "slow-starter" team.

269
00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:01,610
They perform better in the 
second quarter than the first.

270
00:16:01,610 --> 00:16:04,150
Same for the second half of the game overall.

271
00:16:04,150 --> 00:16:06,730
The level of intense play that 
they bring to the court at their

272
00:16:06,730 --> 00:16:08,320
peak is something to be scared of.

273
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:11,080
Hold up. How'd you get your 
hands on that, anyway?

274
00:16:11,710 --> 00:16:14,960
Taro gave it to me. Or 
rather, forced it on me.

275
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:19,480
Our defensive strategy worked well 
in the first quarter, but that's

276
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:21,000
not going to be enough to win.

277
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:24,460
Starting in the second quarter,
we'll put on more of an offensive.

278
00:16:24,830 --> 00:16:26,780
This should be obvious to all of you,

279
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:29,160
but we want to score without 
letting them score.

280
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:32,170
If we can't manage that,
then we won't be able to win in the end.

281
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:35,880
Yasuhara will be subbing in for Nabe.

282
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:37,140
S-sure.

283
00:16:37,790 --> 00:16:40,460
Natsume, please provide 
him with your support.

284
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:42,420
I already know what I need to do.

285
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:46,880
Kurumatani, keep up your aggressive defense
and aim to get some steals.

286
00:16:48,290 --> 00:16:49,880
Whenever making a fast break for the basket

287
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:52,040
isn't an option, Chiaki 
will be our rallying point.

288
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,250
Am I understood?

289
00:16:53,250 --> 00:16:54,570
Loud and clear.

290
00:16:58,130 --> 00:17:03,000
I was very curious, since I heard that their manager
was also doubling as their coach.

291
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,750
She's quite the tactician,
far more competent than I ever expected.

292
00:17:07,290 --> 00:17:10,710
For now, let's just see what happens
when I play into their hand.

293
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:13,290
Taro. Here's the plan.

294
00:17:13,290 --> 00:17:15,670
You don't need bother trying
to score any more points, okay?

295
00:17:16,790 --> 00:17:17,880
What?!

296
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,540
Have you gone senile on us, Gramps?!

297
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:23,140
If I'm not going to score us 
points, then who the hell is?!

298
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:27,540
Cut me some slack. You can't shake off
that short kid at all, can you?

299
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:30,520
Running around like a madman
is only going to wear you out.

300
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:31,830
That's not enough to stop me!

301
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:34,790
The interval is now over!

302
00:17:34,790 --> 00:17:36,390
Huh? Already?!

303
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:38,210
Give 'em hell, Yasu!

304
00:17:38,210 --> 00:17:40,960
Get out there and show them
what a supporting character can do!

305
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,540
I'm a main character, dammit!

306
00:17:43,670 --> 00:17:45,210
Um, Momoharu?

307
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:48,330
Is something wrong? Everyone's 
already on the court.

308
00:17:48,830 --> 00:17:50,210
Oh... right.

309
00:17:55,170 --> 00:17:57,380
Throw-in with Kuzu High in possession!

310
00:17:57,790 --> 00:18:01,250
Why did you say all that 
stuff to Taro, coach?

311
00:18:01,630 --> 00:18:03,960
You know that's only going 
to get him all wound up!

312
00:18:04,330 --> 00:18:06,170
Ehhh, don't fret about it.

313
00:18:06,170 --> 00:18:08,380
That's exactly why I gave him a hard time
in the first place.

314
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:09,100
Huh?

315
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:12,500
Kuzuryu! Kuzuryu!

316
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:16,040
Kuzuryu! Kuzuryu!

317
00:18:16,710 --> 00:18:18,630
His eyes just never stop moving.

318
00:18:19,250 --> 00:18:21,200
He's keeping a sharp watch for any openings.

319
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:24,210
As a fellow point guard, I've 
really gotta hand it to him.

320
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:27,160
This guy is a legit passing specialist!

321
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:28,370
Peep.

322
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:35,210
You know, Chiaki keeps glancing over here
every so often. Why is that?

323
00:18:35,210 --> 00:18:36,300
Beats me.

324
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:41,010
Okay, I've exuded enough charisma.
It's time to strut my stuff.

325
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,670
He's trying to drive past me?

326
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:50,210
But considering his big size,
I doubt he's actually that fast.

327
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:53,500
Does he seriously think he can cut through
with a spin like that?

328
00:18:55,210 --> 00:18:56,320
I don't see the ball!

329
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:58,530
Did he lose it?! Where'd it go?!

330
00:18:58,530 --> 00:19:00,040
Kato! Above you!

331
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:03,620
It was a pass?!

332
00:19:04,290 --> 00:19:08,580
He coordinated with the center
to get that pass through while in my blind spot?!

333
00:19:09,790 --> 00:19:10,500
Go!

334
00:19:14,630 --> 00:19:16,900
His timing is absolutely sensational.

335
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:19,420
Just one misstep and that would have been
a foul for sure.

336
00:19:19,790 --> 00:19:21,460
Look! Yasu's wide open!

337
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:22,830
Score us some points!

338
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:39,920
All right! We took the lead!

339
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:42,580
Hell yeah! We're a force to be reckoned with!

340
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,330
Jeez, I gotta do everything around here.

341
00:19:46,250 --> 00:19:50,040
Those were all smooth moves,
from in the back and up to the basket!

342
00:19:50,750 --> 00:19:52,830
I can't believe how coordinated 
those plays were!

343
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:57,000
I nearly forgot. Those two are twin brothers!

344
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:59,580
Our point guard and our center.

345
00:20:00,290 --> 00:20:02,290
I don't think there's ever been a better duo!

346
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:06,080
I was a little worried about Momoharu
because of how he was acting.

347
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:08,520
But I guess I was just 
reading too much into it.

348
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:13,170
Katori! They haven't gotten 
their zone defense up yet!

349
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,040
Oh shit!

350
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:16,710
Okay! Let's make a fast 
break and tear them apart!

351
00:20:19,290 --> 00:20:21,500
Just watch me, you damn pipsqueak!

352
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:23,860
I'm DEFINITELY going to 
leave you in the dust!

353
00:20:25,210 --> 00:20:27,500
Acceleration Mode.... on!

354
00:20:31,290 --> 00:20:33,170
What the hell was that, dude?!

355
00:20:33,170 --> 00:20:35,210
I didn't see him coming 
because he's so damn small!

356
00:20:36,170 --> 00:20:36,670
Shit!

357
00:20:40,670 --> 00:20:41,630
Oh crap!

358
00:20:41,630 --> 00:20:43,500
Yasuhara! Go for it again!

359
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:45,970
Stop!

360
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:48,580
Your layup form is all wrong.

361
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:51,830
What your hands are doing is more important
than how you jump.

362
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:54,380
After you jump, have the 
ball roll over your fingers.

363
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:58,750
Then all you have to do is... let 
it fall right into the basket.

364
00:21:11,450 --> 00:21:13,910
You did it! That was awesome, Yasuha-

365
00:21:17,130 --> 00:21:19,710
Hoo boy, they've really 
got us on the ropes now!

366
00:21:19,710 --> 00:21:22,330
Don't make it sound like we've already lost!

367
00:21:22,330 --> 00:21:24,260
We're just getting started! Isn't that right?

368
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:27,800
I'm impressed, the other team
has some incredible players on their roster.

369
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,170
Come on, Coach!

370
00:21:29,170 --> 00:21:32,270
We're in a tight spot, 
I'm not sure what to do.

371
00:21:32,790 --> 00:21:34,500
I guess maybe we should 
put Taro on the bench.

372
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:37,100
I can hear you from over here, damn geezer!

373
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:39,330
Just shut up and watch.

374
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:42,570
Forget that shorty, I'm gonna 
fly past their whole team!

375
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:44,830
Oh crap, now he's even more wound up.

376
00:21:44,830 --> 00:21:47,780
He's gonna go on a rampage 
soon, there's no doubt.

377
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:50,630
And I keep telling you, 
that's exactly what we want.

378
00:21:50,630 --> 00:21:51,490
Huh?

379
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:57,420
We're going to have Taro...
trample all over that kid's tiny wings.

380
00:23:30,930 --> 00:23:35,390
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Versus

381
00:23:31,670 --> 00:23:34,080
Next time: "Versus."

